{{! Post-save warning banner: the save went through, but the content references files nobody has
    uploaded and/or links pages nobody has written. Purely informational and dismissable — each
    reference starts working the moment its file is uploaded / page is created, with no further edit
    here, which is why saving is never blocked over it. Shown on the page view and on the editor
    (staged saves land back there); the whole block is gated by refWarn, and the model keys come from
    refWarningModel in WikiRouting. The sentence-and-lists live in ONE flex-item <div> beside the icon
    (see the view.hbs note on gap-2 inserting gaps between every loose child). }}
{{#refWarn}}
<div class="alert alert-warning alert-dismissible d-flex align-items-start gap-2 py-2" role="alert">
    <div>
        <p><span class="fw-bolder">Page saved, but note that some file or page references have nothing located at their destination.</span> Ignore if you plan to add or leave as-is, or fix if this is a mistake:</p>
        <ul class="mt-1 mb-0">
            {{#refWarnHasAssets}}<li>Assets: {{#refWarnAssets}}<code>{{.}}</code> {{/refWarnAssets}}</li>{{/refWarnHasAssets}}
            {{! Comma-separated: each non-first item leads with ", " (the `first` flag comes from the
                model), so no trailing separator to strip. }}
            {{#refWarnHasPages}}<li>Pages: {{#refWarnPages}}{{^first}}, {{/first}}<a href="{{createUrl}}" title="Create this page"><code>{{label}}</code></a>{{/refWarnPages}}</li>{{/refWarnHasPages}}
        </ul>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="alert" aria-label="Dismiss"></button>
</div>
{{/refWarn}}
